{
	"_readme": [
		"A map is ASCII rows plus a legend. Two layers share one grid: 'ground' is what you",
		"walk on, 'decor' is what stands on top of it (a space means nothing there).",
		"",
		"Whether a tile blocks movement is NOT decided here - it comes from the tiles' own",
		"data, so making cliffs solid is an art decision and the movement code never learns",
		"the word 'cliff'.",
		"",
		"Coordinates in spawns, npcs, objects and warps are [column, row], zero-based,",
		"matching the rows below.",
		"",
		"An 'object' is an interaction point, not a sprite: the well below is the water tiles",
		"you can already see, plus four lines saying what happens when you press into them.",
		"",
		"The gap in the north wall is the road to the village. It is the one tile of that",
		"wall a character may stand on, and it is a warp, which is the only reason the map",
		"validator allows an opening in an outer edge at all."
	],
